Heard a wild story from a growth master today that's got me rethinking everything. A small business owner scores a proposal from a Lululemon supplier/manufacturer for this killer new sports bra—amazing texture, perfect shape, cutting-edge tech to support during workouts. Loves it, buys 30,000 units, brands 'em, and launches. But flop: only a few hundred sell. Team's panicking, no budget for big influencers, so they hit up KOCs (key opinion customers—smaller influencers). These folks promote it like: "This bra makes your skin look fairer in photoshoots! (拍照显白)" (classic China vibe ). Team's offended—WTF? No shoutout to the tech or functionality? So unprofessional! Plot twist: 9 out of 10 influencers say the same thing. Overnight? 10,000+ bras sold! Team flips their ads to match, and boom—everything clears out. Moral: We think we know what customers want, but their real desires? Often hidden gems. Got me pondering: When singles gripe about not finding "the one" and say they just want a partner... what's the real demand lurking underneath? We're decoding that as we build 
@Souli_AI
. Any Thoughts? #MarketingTips#SouliAI#GrowthMarketing

