家、普通人接受媒体采访，“新加坡人不是中国人，新加坡是个多元种族社会”。[黑线]外媒炒作这事有完没完？ L盖世英雄玉椒龙的微博视频」 **English Translation:** “Singapore belongs to the Indians, not to you. @//Great Hero Jade Pepper Dragon Because of *A Letter to Amah*, Singaporean experts and ordinary people gave media interviews saying ‘Singaporeans are not Chinese; Singapore is a multi-ethnic society’. [black lines] Will foreign media never stop hyping this?” **Analytical Function:** The core debate concerns Singaporean national identity and Chinese-Singaporean relations. “Indians” are deployed as a provocative rhetorical replacement for the “real” owners, turning an identity discussion into an ethnic taunt. ### 1.4 Cancel Culture / “Indian Son-in-Law” **Mandarin Original (excerpt):** 「…//@心医林霖:别离，离了又要从老实人身上，把给印度人的钱和房，坑回来。应该带女方直接回印度 展开c @纯良软妹 印度女婿」 **English Translation (excerpt):** “…@//Heart-Doctor Lin Lin: Don’t divorce; if you separate, then the money and house given to the Indian will end up being squeezed back out of honest people. You should just take the woman directly back to India… @//Pure-Heart Soft Girl Indian son-in-law.” **Analytical Function:** The underlying issue is a personal scandal and property/financial dispute. The label “Indian son-in-law” (or “Indian”) serves as a stigmatizing ethnic marker that amplifies moral condemnation and justifies extreme suggested actions. --- Chapter 2 – India as Actual Topic (Often Hostile, but Central) Here India or Indians are genuinely the subject: policy, economic, military, or cultural discussions framed around India itself. ### 2.1 Visa Policy and “Indian Hidden Danger” **Mandarin Original:** 「拒绝印度隐患！拒绝社会风险！ @韦墨Pro 请神容易送神难！欧美国家都在收紧对印度人的入境政策，咱们却在2025年给印度公民发了近40万份签证，占全年签证总量的20%，可中印贸易额只占中国总贸易额的2.4%。 更扎眼的是：政策看着挺"友好"，风险却先找上门。中国驻印度大使徐飞洪高调说过，3个多月就签发超8.5万份签证，还把签证受理外包给VFS G…」 **English Translation:** “Reject Indian hidden dangers! Reject social risk! @//Wei Mo Pro It is easy to invite a god but hard to send one away! European and American countries are tightening entry policies toward Indians, yet in 2025 we gave nearly 400,000 visas to Indian citizens, 20% of all visas that year, while China-India trade accounts for only 2.4% of China’s total trade. Even more striking: the policy looks quite ‘friendly’, yet the risks came first. China’s ambassador to India, Xu Feihong, proudly said that in just over three months over 85,000 visas had been issued, and visa acceptance was outsourced to VFS G…” **Analytical Function:** India is the explicit policy object. Hostility is expressed through a “risk” and “hidden danger” frame that contrasts visa numbers with low trade volume and warns of future problems. ### 2.2 Comparative Development: China vs India **Mandarin Original (headline + commentary):** 「@南亚研究通讯 为什么中国起飞，印度掉队？答案或许不在1978年… @第三人造天堂 从周公到毛都缺，四千年都过在狗身上了…//@萱叔宝:印度缺一个毛」 **English Translation:** “@//South Asia Research Communications Why did China take off while India fell behind? The answer may not lie in 1978… @//Third Artificial Heaven From Duke Zhou to Mao they have none; four thousand years all spent on dogs… //@//Xuanshu Bao: India is missing a Mao.” **Analytical Function:** India is central to a comparative development analysis. Commenters layer historical and political insults on top of the structural discussion. ### 2.3 Defense and Missile Testing **Mandarin Original:** 「2026年6月，印度国防研究与发展组织进行一系列密集的导弹测试。 弹道导弹防御：6月10日至11日，连续进行三次飞行测试，成功验证了多层弹道导弹防御能力。试射的AD-1和AD-2拦截弹展示拦截5000公里级别远程弹道导弹及洲际导弹的能力。 远程对地攻击：6月15日，成功试射国产远程对地攻击巡航导弹（LRLAC …」 **English Translation:** “In June 2026, India’s Defense Research and Development Organization carried out a series of intensive missile tests. Ballistic missile defense: from June 10 to 11, three consecutive flight tests were conducted, successfully verifying multi-layer ballistic missile defense capability. The tested AD-1 and AD-2 interceptors demonstrated the ability to intercept 5,000-kilometer-class long-range ballistic missiles and intercontinental missiles. Long-range ground attack: on June 15, it successfully test-fired an indigenous long-range ground-attack cruise missile (LRLAC …” **Analytical Function:** India’s military capability and recent testing activity are the direct subject. The post is informational in tone but sits within a broader context of strategic attention. ### 2.4 Industry and Localization – PV (Photovoltaics) **Mandarin Original:** 「王新喜TMT 发布了头条文章：《投入1700亿美金，印度光伏的本土化玩砸了，这一次，中企不该帮了》」 **English Translation:** “Wang Xinxi TMT published a headline article: ‘After investing 170 billion US dollars, India’s localization of photovoltaics has flopped; this time, Chinese enterprises should not help.’” **Analytical Function:** India’s industrial policy and the outcome of large-scale localization efforts in the photovoltaic sector are explicitly central. The framing advises Chinese companies against further involvement. --- Chapter 3 – Security, Migration, and Visas This chapter focuses on the security/migration field, where India is invoked as a risk (sometimes as the central topic, sometimes as a taunt). ### 3.1 Outsourcing Visa Checks in India **Mandarin Original:** 「有传说，驻印度使馆把入华签证审核外包给第三方，导致大量造假材料的印度人入境。」 **English Translation:** “There is a rumor that the embassy in India has outsourced visa vetting for entering China to a third party, resulting in large numbers of Indians with falsified documents entering [China].” **Analytical Function:** The post alleges a procedural vulnerability in visa processing that allegedly enables fraudulent entry. India/Indians are framed as the source of the security risk. ### 3.2 Fingerprint Policy and “引入印度人” **Mandarin Original (thread + comment):** 「@博弈的逻辑 对印鉴证发放不录指纹最不理解，如果一个印度人来中国后撕掉鉴证黑下来，怎么遣返？ 录个指纹，也就是几秒钟的事情。取消录入指纹，节省不下多少时间，但却会带来很大的问题。如果一个印度人来中国后撕掉鉴证，死活不说自己身份，那么怎么遣返？ 真正让人担心的，不是办证环节少一道手续这么简单，而 … @用心去看13 而我们却照做，混乱在后面//@龙的传人原沙和尚的微博01:别人的目标就是引入印度人。」 **English Translation (combined):** “@//Logic of Game What I least understand is the decision not to collect fingerprints for India-related visas; if an Indian person comes to China and tears up the visa and stays black [illegally], how will we deport them? Recording a fingerprint only takes a few seconds. Removing fingerprinting saves hardly any time, but it will create great problems. If an Indian person comes to China, tears up the visa, and stubbornly refuses to state their identity, then how can we deport them? What truly worries people is not ‘just one less step’ in the documentation process… @Look with Your Heart 13 And we actually follow along and do this; chaos lies ahead. //
@Original
 Monk of the Dragon’s Descendants: Other people’s goal is precisely to bring Indians in.” **Analytical Function:** A specific visa administration decision (no fingerprint collection) is criticized through the hypothetical scenario of Indian overstays. The comment escalates the concern into a conspiracy claim that the policy intentionally facilitates Indian entry. ### 3.3 “No Guns or Cannons, Only Visas” **Mandarin Original:** 「然后印度阿三被一群人放进来了，不用枪炮，只要签证！ @当一个科学家 印度这个蛆国，下手是很阴的。我们三年自然灾害，他袭我边境；三年“疫情”时，又搞斑公湖；印蛆历来是趁你病要你命，一点不含糊的无耻小人之国。」 **English Translation:** “And then Indian ‘Ah-san’ were let in by a whole bunch of people; no guns or cannons needed, only visas! @//Be a Scientist India, this maggot country, strikes in a very sneaky way. During our three years of natural disasters, it attacked our border; during three years of ‘epidemic’, it stirred up Pangong Lake; Indian maggots have always been a shameless petty nation that takes your life when you are sick, without any hesitation.” **Analytical Function:** Visa policy and alleged historical border incidents are fused with extreme dehumanizing language (“maggot country,” “Indian maggots”). The post portrays Indian entry via visas as a covert form of aggression. ### 3.4 Everyday Security Encounter – Hong Kong/Shenzhen Border Check **Mandarin Original:** 「我擦~不是不欢迎印度人，是不欢迎喜欢白嫖，霍霍中国的阿三来#印度人在中国# @大象观点 2026年6月9日，香港海关（准备入境深圳），3名印度男性游客准备入关，海关例行检查，他们从香港过关去深圳，海关按规定要三样东西：有效签证（他们有旅游签），返程机票，足够现金/资金证明，而他们的回答是： 海关：“返程机票呢？”答：没有，没买。 海关：“身上带了多少钱？”答：一分钱都没有， …」 **English Translation:** “Damn ~ it is not that we don’t welcome Indians; it’s that we don’t welcome ‘Ah-san’ who love freeloading and wrecking China #Indians in China# @//Elephant Viewpoint On June 9, 2026, at Hong Kong Customs (about to enter Shenzhen), three Indian male tourists prepared to enter; Customs carried out a routine inspection. They were crossing from Hong Kong into Shenzhen. According to regulations, Customs requires three things: a valid visa (they had tourist visas), return tickets, and sufficient cash/funds proof. Their answers: Customs: ‘Where are your return tickets?’ They replied: ‘None, we didn’t buy them.’ Customs: ‘How much money do you have on you?’ They replied: ‘Not a single cent,’ …” **Analytical Function:** A concrete border-control anecdote is used to illustrate and reinforce the broader claim that Indian visitors represent an economic and security risk (freeloading, lack of funds, potential overstays). --- Chapter 4 – Economy and Industry Narratives This chapter gathers posts concerning FDI, photovoltaics (PV), manufacturing, and corporate investment decisions related to India. ### 4.1 FDI Collapse **Mandarin Original:** 「持续抢劫外资，终于让印度迎来了反噬，一年的外资投资只剩下3.5亿美元了……[允悲]#烽火问鼎计划#」 **English Translation:** “Constantly robbing foreign capital has finally brought backlash upon India; its annual foreign investment has dropped to only 350 million US dollars… [sob] #Fenghuo Winning the Throne Plan#.” **Analytical Function:** India’s declining FDI is presented as karmic retribution for alleged mistreatment of foreign investors. The tone is celebratory of India’s economic difficulties. ### 4.2 Tech/Industry Transfer Complaints **Mandarin Original:** 「保变电工，手把手教印度人，恐怕学不会，一批批派外派技术人员从基础教起……[doge]」 **Comment:** 「不仅仅是资敌，更是贱到没底线」 **English Translation:** “Baobian Electric Workers, hand-in-hand teaching Indians; I’m afraid they still may not learn, sending batch after batch of expatriate technical staff starting from the basics… [doge]. Not just supporting the enemy financially; it is lowly with no bottom line.” **Analytical Function:** Knowledge transfer and technical training provided to Indian partners are framed as both futile (“they still may not learn”) and morally culpable (“supporting the enemy,” “lowly with no bottom line”). ### 4.3 Aluminum and Energy **Mandarin Original (excerpt):** 「全球的电解铝企业都是跟低成本能源分不开的 中国产量4500万吨，全球第一… 印度420万吨，全球第二，低成本动力煤 俄罗斯380万吨，全球第三…」 **English Translation (excerpt):** “Global electrolytic aluminum enterprises are inseparable from low-cost energy. China’s output is 45 million tons, ranked first in the world… India’s is 4.2 million tons, ranked second, with low-cost thermal coal. Russia’s is 3.8 million tons, ranked third…” **Analytical Function:** A comparative industrial ranking that places India second globally in electrolytic aluminum production due to low-cost coal. The post is largely factual but embedded in competitive national-industry discourse. ### 4.4 “惠印” (Favoring India) and Corporate Investment Criticism **Mandarin Original:** 「@‌惠科股份（HKC）‌ 你们公司是缺钱还是缺德了，外资都在从印度撤离，你们还送钱去，就你们聪明，要提前布局，趁着印度设套没收网时去挣点外快。祝王智勇和全体管理管理人员能挣到钱，好能送你们老婆去欧美印三通一达。」 **English Translation:** “@//HKC – is your company short of money or short of morals? Foreign capital is pulling out of India, yet you are still sending money there. You’re the clever ones, laying out early, going to earn some petty cash right when India is setting up a trap before pulling in the net. I wish Wang Zhiyong and the whole management can make money, so they can send their wives to Europe/US/India by ‘Three Links and One Arrival’.” **Analytical Function:** Corporate investment in India is condemned on both economic (“India is setting a trap”) and moral (“short of morals”) grounds. The post personalizes criticism toward company executives. --- Chapter 5 – Culture-War and Symbolic Purity This chapter groups posts involving cultural symbols, consumer boycotts, and identity claims involving Indian elements (yoga, food, restaurants, Singapore identity, etc.). ### 5.1 Lululemon Great Wall “Stacking” Formula **Mandarin Original:** 「#lululemon 日本太鼓# 这件事最吊诡的是在于： 一个加拿大品牌在中国的长城上，用日本的太鼓，宣传印度的瑜伽。 简直就是不注意文化和当地人情感的品牌错配宣传反面典型。」 **English Translation:** “#lululemon Japanese Taiko# The most bizarre part of this incident is: A Canadian brand, on the Great Wall of China, uses Japanese taiko to promote Indian yoga. It is simply a negative textbook case of mismatched branding that does not pay attention to culture and local people’s feelings.” **Analytical Function:** The post criticizes a brand activation as culturally insensitive “stacking” (Canadian brand + Japanese drums + Indian yoga on Chinese heritage site). It frames the combination as a violation of symbolic and national-cultural boundaries. ### 5.2 “Japan + India Yoga = Bad” **Mandarin Original:** 「#lululemon股价累计大跌超76%#日本、印度瑜伽，呵，肯定不是好东西。」 **English Translation:** “#lululemon’s share price has cumulatively fallen more than 76%# Japanese, Indian yoga—heh, it definitely isn’t anything good.” **Analytical Function:** A terse, dismissive linkage of “Japanese + Indian yoga” as inherently negative, using the brand’s stock performance as supposed evidence. ### 5.3 “以倭代华” and Promoting Indian Yoga on the Great Wall **Mandarin Original:** 「弄个以倭代华的东西，在长城上推广印度人的瑜伽，然后说致敬中国文化……我可去尼玛吧。」 **English Translation:** “Create some ‘using the Japanese to replace the Chinese’ thing, promote Indians’ yoga on the Great Wall, and then say it is to pay tribute to Chinese culture… I’ll go to hell with that.” **Analytical Function:** The activation is read as a double substitution (“Japanese instead of Chinese” + Indian yoga), framed as an insult to Chinese cultural sovereignty and authenticity. ### 5.4 Indian Restaurants, Boycott, and “Four-No Principles” **Mandarin Original (excerpt):** 「印度媳妇丹丹的餐厅没人了，大中午的饭点都没人，冷清的可怕，从前排队两小时才能吃上饭，现在已经没了往日的辉煌，他们夫妻俩连账号都停更了，印度员工也离开了。 ​大家自发遵守了“四不原则”，你开你的，我不吃就是了，不进店，不消费，甚至连账号都没人看了，所以，账号也就没有流量了。」 **English Translation (excerpt):** “Indian wife Dandan’s restaurant has no people; even at lunchtime there’s no one, the emptiness is frightening. Before you had to queue two hours to eat there; now the former glory is gone. The couple have even stopped updating their account, and the Indian employees have left. Everyone spontaneously follows the ‘four-no principles’: you open your place, I simply won’t eat there; don’t enter, don’t spend, people don’t even look at their account anymore, so naturally the account has no traffic.” **Analytical Function:** A narrative of successful consumer boycott against an Indian-associated restaurant. The “four-no principles” (don’t enter, don’t spend, don’t engage, don’t give traffic) are presented as effective grassroots punishment. ### 5.5 Indian Food as Neutral/Positive Counterpoint **Mandarin Original:** 「第一次吃印度菜咖喱超话 好评[举手] 2北京·爱在咖喱(天坛店)」 **English Translation:** “First time eating Indian food (curry super-topic). Good review [raised hand] at Love Curry (Tiantan branch), Beijing.” **Analytical Function:** A rare positive or at least neutral consumer post about Indian cuisine. Useful as contrast to the dominant slur-driven or boycott-oriented discourse in the dataset. --- Chapter 6 – Racialized Everyday Life and Body/Odor Rhetoric This chapter concentrates narratives involving pools, trains, taxis, smell, hand-eating, and similar everyday settings where India/Indians are reduced to a body/odor stereotype. ### 6.1 Pool Anecdote – “Engraved in Indians’ DNA” **Mandarin Original:** 「刻在印度人DNA里的，有水就要下去搓澡 @四字网友 想起我小时候在嘉和苑游泳，来了几个阿三，门口要他们出示相关票据…他们叽里呱啦说一通，大致意思就是，不游，只是路过来看看…阿三进去后 …」 **English Translation (main line):** “Engraved in Indians’ DNA is that whenever there is water, they must get in to scrub themselves. @//Four-Character Netizen It reminds me of when I was a child swimming at Jiaheyuan; a few ‘Ah-san’ came, the gate asked them to show their tickets… They babbled a bit, meaning they ‘would not swim, just pass by to take a look’… After the ‘Ah-san’ went in …” **Analytical Function:** A childhood swimming-pool memory is repurposed into a generalized racial stereotype about hygiene and behavior (“engraved in DNA”). The anecdote serves to naturalize the claim that Indians have an innate, problematic relationship with water and cleanliness. ### 6.2 Train Car Smell and Bare Feet **Mandarin Original (two posts):** 「#印度人# @一纸琉涟 一名网友在去往张家界旅途中拍摄的一幕，网友带着孩子一进车厢，就闻到了一股浓烈刺鼻的气味，即使带着口罩，也阻挡不了那股气味钻进鼻腔里。 走到车厢内部，才发现，原来是每排座位，都躺着一名脱了鞋的印度人在睡觉，没有横排躺下的，也都脱了鞋子，把脚搭在对面的座位上休息。 后来男子实在忍受不了 …」 **Comment:** 「好文塾: 印度富人都忍受不了印度穷人，凭什么要中国人来闻那个臭味。印度自己国家的人都嫌弃印度穷人，说明确实一塌糊涂。印度穷人出国，就是为了传播印度味，让全世界人知道印度人臭成什么鬼样子。[酷][阴险]」 **English Translation (joined):** “#Indians# @//One Sheet of Flowing Ripple A netizen shot this scene on a journey to Zhangjiajie. The netizen entered the carriage with their child and immediately smelled a strong, sharp stench; even wearing a mask couldn’t stop the smell from drilling into the nostrils. Walking further into the carriage, it turned out that on each row of seats, one Indian who had taken off his shoes and was sleeping; those not lying across the row had also taken off his shoes and put their feet up on the opposite seat to rest. Later the man simply couldn’t bear it… @//Good-Writing Cram School: Even India’s rich can’t stand India’s poor; why should Chinese people have to smell that stink? That Indians themselves despise their poor shows how utterly messed up it really is. Indian poor going abroad is just to spread ‘Indian smell’, to let the whole world know how disgustingly stinky Indians are.” **Analytical Function:** A train-travel anecdote about smell and bare feet is generalized into a national/racial odor stereotype. The comment escalates it by claiming that even Indians dislike their own poor and that Indian migrants deliberately “spread Indian smell” abroad. ### 6.3 Taxi Refusal and “Too Smelly” **Mandarin Original:** 「@一纸琉涟 【近期有一印度博主】在云南赶车被拒，原因是太臭了。印度博主在云南连拦3俩车都被师傅们拒绝了，师傅们都说印度人太臭了，给多少钱师傅们都说不愿意拉印度人。 我认为师傅们做得对，都不拉印度人，让他们自己走路，最好的是不要来，如果是换成我开网络车，遇到印度人我也不会拉他们。 他们实在太臭了」 **English Translation:** “@//One Sheet of Flowing Ripple [Recently there was an Indian blogger] who in Yunnan tried to catch rides but was refused, because he was too smelly. The Indian blogger in Yunnan flagged down three cars in a row and was refused by all the drivers; the drivers all said Indians are too smelly, and no matter how much money he gave, they were not willing to take Indians. I think the drivers did the right thing; don’t take Indians at all, let them walk by themselves, and best of all is for them not to come. If it were me driving a ride-hailing car, if I met Indians I would not take them either. They are really too smelly.” **Analytical Function:** An alleged real-world refusal of service to an Indian person is celebrated and generalized. The post endorses discrimination on the basis of an essentialized “Indian smell” and explicitly advises against any interaction or entry. ### 6.4 Hand-Eating and Imagined Hygiene **Mandarin Original:** 「印度飞饼 我吃过一次 真的是印度人 然后… 我开始思考他们是不是用手擦粑粑了 [泪][泪]」 **English Translation:** “Indian flying bread (roti). I ate it once. It really was made by Indians. And then… I began to wonder whether they used their hands to wipe poop. [tears] [tears]”

CHARGES LAID We have charged a woman with 7 offences after locating more than $150,000 of stolen Lululemon merchandise, along with drugs, cash & other stolen property, during a search of a northeast Calgary residence. On Wednesday, May 20, 2026, at approx. 7:55 a.m., we attended a residence in the 300 block of Herron Mews N.E. to conduct a curfew compliance check. The resident failed to answer the door, placing her in breach of court-ordered release conditions. The following morning, on Thursday, May 21, 2026, at about 9:45 a.m., officers returned to the residence to execute an arrest warrant for the breach. The suspect exited the residence & was taken into custody. While inside the residence, officers observed drugs, cash & suspected stolen property in plain view. The home was secured & a search warrant was obtained & executed later the same day. The following items were located & seized: Stolen Lululemon merchandise, with an estimated value of more than $150,000, believed to have been stolen during transport. More than $10,000 cash 430 grams of methamphetamine with an estimated street value of $8,660 6 grams of cocaine with an estimated street value of $610 380 grams of cutting agent 24 packages of illegal tobacco 12 rounds of live pistol ammunition Dozens of suspected stolen identification documents Property linked to previously reported break-ins, including perfume, beauty products & a coin collection Cassandra Ruby ST ONGE, 35, of Calgary, has been charged with: 2 counts of possession of a controlled substance for the purpose of trafficking 1 count of possession of stolen property obtained by crime over $5,000 1 count possession of stolen property obtained by crime under $5,000 1 count of possession of proceeds of crime over $5,000 1 count of possession of an identity document 1 count of possession of a prohibited weapon She will next appear in court on Friday, June 19, 2026. Anyone with information about this incident is asked to contact police by calling the non-emergency number. Information? CPS: 403-266-1234 
